, is an American rapper and actor. Along with his manager, Chaka Zulu, Ludacris is the co-founder of [l=Disturbing Tha Peace], an imprint distributed by [l=Def Jam Recordings]. Ludacris has sold 17 million albums in the United States and 24 million records sold worldwide, and he has won the Screen Actors Guild, Critic's Choice, MTV, and Grammy Awards during his career.\r\n\r\nBorn in Champaign, Illinois, of African American and Native American descent. Luda wrote his first rap song at age nine when moving to Atlanta and joined an amateur rap group three years later. He attended Banneker High School in Atlanta, Georgia. From 1998 to 1999, and studied music management at Georgia State University.\r\n\r\nLudacris worked as a radio editor under the pseudonym \"DJ Chris Lova Lova\" at Atlanta hip hop station HOT 97.5 FM WHTA, now located at 107.9 FM, when producer and rapper [a=Timbaland] made an offer for Ludacris to work with him at the radio station, leading to his performance on the track \"Phat Rabbit\" on Timbaland's 1998 album Tim's Bio: Life from da Bassment.\r\n\r\nLudacris released his major label debut, \"Back for the First Time\", in October 2000. This album was actually a modified re-release of the album \"Incognegro\", made in 1998. It was produced with the help of the underground producer Sessy Melia, whom he dated for a short while. The album reached as high as #4 on the U.S. Billboard 200, and was a major success. Ludacris made his mark on the industry with singles such as \"Southern Hospitality\" and \"What's Your Fantasy\", along with his first ever single the \"Phat Rabbit\", from two years prior. Guest appearances included [a=4-Ize], [a=I-20], [a=Shawnna], [a=Pastor Troy], [a=Timbaland], [a=Trina], [a=Foxy Brown], [a=UGK], and others. Ludacris stated in an interview on MTV's hip hop program Direct Effect that he came up with his stage name based on his \"split personality\" that he considered \"ridiculous\" and \"ludicrous\".\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:36100","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":645333,"name":"Christopher Bridges"},{"id":9196039,"name":"Chris Lova Lova"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Christopher Bridges","Ladacris","Luacris","Lucradis","Luda","Luda Chris","Luda Vs. Idris","Ludaccris","Ludachris","Ludacirs","Ludacri$","Ludacric","Ludacris (Fatboy Slim Remix)","Ludacris\"","Ludacriss","Ludakris","Ludcris","Ludichris","Ludicris","Ludicrous AKA Chris Lova Lova","Ludicrus","Ludracis","リュダクリス","路達克里斯"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/36100-Ludacris","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.ludaversal.com","http://www.facebook.com/Ludacris","http://www.instagram.com/ludacris","http://twitter.com/Ludacris","http://www.youtube.com/dtprecordstv","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludacris"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/417/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"417","image":"https://i.discogs.com/hYfNfl6LtPKDWNQXjwuEQNtzmnMTYI9kD9EZwaMK-Q0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:399/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQxNy0x/NTEyNDMxODYzLTk5/ODQucG5n.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/3FV106Qpi1HhpQ6O2DhEgBjWYhWdrkT09YW9PPk1E5M/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQxNy0x/NTEyNDMxODYzLTk5/ODQucG5n.jpeg","profile":"UK producer and musician.\r\nBorn 6 September 1971 in St Albans, England\r\n\r\nA fixture on the UK jungle scene since the early nineties, Photek a.k.a. Rupert Parkes (associated with Ipswich in the nineties) is best known for his role in developing the \"intelligent\" drum & bass genre. ","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:417","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":652,"name":"Special Forces"},{"id":2015,"name":"Aquarius"},{"id":9815,"name":"Code Of Practice"},{"id":12174,"name":"System X"},{"id":16036,"name":"Phaze 1"},{"id":16982,"name":"Studio Pressure"},{"id":32470,"name":"Synthetics"},{"id":37745,"name":"The Truper"},{"id":47561,"name":"The Sentinel"},{"id":243991,"name":"Rupert Parkes"},{"id":2681719,"n